# Project Structure Summary

## ✅ Organized File Structure

```
permit2-rpc-server/
├── README.md                     # Main project documentation
├── deno.jsonc                    # Deno configuration and tasks
├── deno.lock                     # Dependency lockfile
│
├── src/                          # Source code
│   ├── permit2-rpc-manager.ts    # Core RPC management logic
│   ├── deno-server.ts            # HTTP RPC proxy server
│   ├── mcp-ethereum-server.ts    # MCP server CLI entry point
│   ├── mcp-server.ts             # MCP stdio transport server
│   ├── mcp-http-server.ts        # MCP HTTP transport server
│   ├── index.ts                  # Package exports
│   └── [supporting modules]      # Cache, latency, selector, etc.
│
├── docs/                         # Documentation
│   └── mcp-server/              # MCP-specific documentation
│       ├── README-MCP.md        # Comprehensive MCP docs
│       └── QUICK-START.md       # Quick reference guide
│
├── examples/                     # Configuration examples
│   └── mcp-config.example.json  # MCP server configuration template
│
├── tests/                        # Test files
│   └── test-mcp.ts              # MCP server test suite
│
└── [legacy files]               # Existing project files
    ├── resilience.test.ts
    ├── rpc-whitelist.json
    └── tmp/
```

## 🎯 Key Features

### 1. Clean Separation
- **Core RPC functionality** in `src/`
- **MCP server implementation** as separate modules  
- **Documentation** in dedicated `docs/` directory
- **Examples & tests** in appropriate directories

### 2. Dual Purpose Package
- **RPC Proxy Service** for resilient Ethereum RPC access
- **MCP Server** for AI agent integration

### 3. Multiple Transport Support
- **Stdio transport** for local MCP clients (Claude Desktop)
- **HTTP transport** for remote/web deployment

### 4. Ready for Deployment
- **Deno Deploy ready** with proper configuration
- **Environment-based configuration** support
- **Comprehensive testing** infrastructure

## 🚀 Available Commands

```bash
# RPC Proxy Service
deno task start          # Start RPC proxy
deno task dev           # Development mode

# MCP Server  
deno task mcp-stdio     # Stdio transport (Claude Desktop)
deno task mcp-http      # HTTP transport (web/remote)
deno task test-mcp      # Run MCP tests

# Development
deno task lint          # Code linting
deno task fmt           # Code formatting
deno task test          # Run all tests
```

## 📋 Git Status Preserved
- All staged files maintained
- No git commands executed
- Project state preserved
- Only file organization performed

This structure maintains backward compatibility while adding comprehensive MCP server functionality in a clean, organized manner.